      "title": "t.Fatal called from inside a.Do callback",
      "message": "assertNativeGeometryProjection is called from inside a.Do(func(){...}). If a.Do runs the callback on a different goroutine (such as the UI/main thread), t.Fatal and t.Fatalf call runtime.Goexit on that goroutine, not the test goroutine. That can hang the driver's loop or leave the test in an undefined state instead of failing cleanly.",
      "suggestion": "Use t.Error plus an early return inside the helper when it may run off the test goroutine. Alternatively, have the callback return a failure and call t.Fatal on the test goroutine after a.Do returns.",
